## Phase 0 — Repo Reconnaissance (MANDATORY SECOND STEP)

Before writing a single line of Robot Framework code, read and internalize from the repo:

### 0.1 — Always Read First
| What to Read | Why |
|---|---|
| Project `README.md` `[profile: readme_path]` | Authoritative folder duties, naming conventions, import patterns |
| Locator/Page files `[profile: pages_dir, variables_dirs]` | Existing locators — **do not redefine** variables already declared |
| Business-flow keyword files `[profile: modules_dir]` | Existing flow keywords — **do not duplicate** |
| Shared/common keyword files `[profile: common_dir]` | Existing setup/teardown, waits, assertions — extend only if genuinely missing |
| Test suites (recursive) `[profile: tests_dir]` | Avoid duplicate test case names and tag collisions |
| Test data files `[profile: data_files]` | Existing data variables — append only; never redefine |

### 0.2 — Repo State Summary (show before any code)

```
## Repo State Summary
- Profile: <path/source of customization layer; "bootstrapped this session" if new>
- README conventions: <key rules extracted>
- Existing Page/locator files: <list>
- Existing Module/flow files: <list>
- Existing Test suites: <list>
- Shared keywords available: <key ones from common layer>
- Data variables available: <relevant ones>
- Profile↔repo mismatches: <none | list>
- GAPS detected: <files/keywords that don't exist yet and will need to be created>
- LOCATOR plan: <reuse from repo | create from screen evidence | GAP placeholders user must fill>
- REUSE plan: <keywords/locators the new scripts will import rather than redefine>
```

> **Rule:** Never emit a `### path` + code fence for a file that already exists and needs no changes. Instead, list it under `REUSE plan` and `Resource` it directly.

