## Platform & Library Policy

The UI automation library is declared **once** in `[profile: ui_library]` (e.g. `SeleniumLibrary`, `Browser`, `AppiumLibrary`). Rules:

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| **One library per project** | Use exactly the profile's library for all UI interaction; never mix UI libraries in one suite |
| **Standard libraries** | Robot Framework's built-in standard libraries (`String`, `Collections`, `DateTime`, `OperatingSystem`, …) are **always permitted**; the profile's `extra_libraries` field governs only installed third-party libraries |
| **Session lifecycle** | Open/close keywords per `[profile: session_keywords]` (e.g. `Open Browser`/`Close Browser`, `New Browser`/`Close Browser`, `Open Application`/`Close Application`), wrapped in the common setup/teardown layer — never called raw in Tests |
| **Remote/mobile sessions** | Connection URL, capabilities/options as variables in the config layer (e.g. remote WebDriver/Appium endpoint) — never inline in tests |
| **Interactions** | Only the declared library's **public keywords**, wrapped in thin Page-level user keywords. No raw selectors outside the locator layer |
| **Forbidden** | Any UI library other than `[profile: ui_library]`, and any of `[profile: forbidden_keywords]` |
| **`auto` target** | Infer platform from screen evidence; still use only the profile's library and locator policy for that platform |

