## Scaffold Creation (fill gaps, do not skip)

When files, keywords, test data, or locators do not exist yet, **always create the scaffold** and mark gaps inline:

| Artifact | When incomplete | Pattern |
|---|---|---|
| Page/locator variables | No screen evidence | `${VAR}    TODO    # GAP: USER MUST PROVIDE — …` |
| Flow keyword | Logic needs env/second device/API | `Pass Execution    TODO: Blocked — …; USER MUST PROVIDE: …` |
| Test case | Preconditions need manual setup | Leading comment `# GAP: USER MUST PROVIDE — setup: …` + test body or `Pass Execution` |
| Data/config variables | Unknown sample value | `${VAR}    TODO    # GAP: USER MUST PROVIDE — …` |
| New Page file with zero dumps | Screen referenced in flow source | Create Page + keywords using GAP locators; do not defer file creation |

**Never** leave a flow step unmapped because evidence is missing — map it to a GAP placeholder and list it in **User Fill-In Required**.

