## Mandatory Files

> **Only emit a file if it is NEW or requires changes.** Files that exist and need no changes: list under `REUSE plan` — do not re-emit them.

The concrete paths come from `[profile: file_map]`. Generic set (core default):

| # | Role | Purpose | Emit when |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 1 | Setup/teardown resource | Session open/close; URL/caps/options vars | Missing **and** the run needs a session, or needs new capability block |
| 2 | Common keywords resource | Shared helpers | The run needs a shared helper that has no home (create or extend) |
| 3 | Wait keywords resource | Library wait wrappers | The run needs a wait wrapper that has no home (create or extend) |
| 4 | Assertion keywords resource | Library assertion wrappers | The run needs an assertion wrapper that has no home (create or extend) |
| 5 | Page file per screen | Locators + screen keywords; no business logic | New screen OR new locators on existing screen |
| 6 | Flow/module file per feature | Business flows; Resources Pages + Common | New feature OR new flows on existing module |
| 7 | Test suite per feature/flow | Test cases; Resources flow layer only; `[Tags]` | Always (new test file per feature/flow) |
| 8 | Test data file | Data placeholders (no secrets) | Missing or new variables needed |

Optional: per-environment configuration file(s) per the profile.

> **A missing-but-unneeded file is not an emit trigger.** If the profile's `file_map` lists a file that does not exist in the repo and the current run needs nothing from it, do not create it — report it once under `Profile↔repo mismatches` in the Repo State Summary.

---

## Duplication Prevention Rules

| Scenario | Action |
|---|---|
| Keyword with same name exists in repo | Reuse it via `Resource`; do not redefine |
| Locator variable already declared in a locator file | Import that file; do not redeclare |
| Test case name already exists in a suite | Append a distinguishing suffix or extend the existing suite file with the new test |
| Setup/teardown resource exists and covers the platform | Reference it; only emit if adding a new capability block |
| Test data file exists | Append new `${VAR}` lines only; never rewrite existing ones |

---

## Deterministic Naming & Structure

Two runs on the same inputs must produce the same file names, keyword names, and structure:

- **Flow/module file name**: derived mechanically from the feature name — the flow source's module/feature column if present, else the flow ID prefix (e.g. `RM-` → `Reminders`), else the first significant noun of the flow title. Singular/plural exactly as it appears in that source; never re-inflect.
- **Page file name**: derived from the screen-evidence file name (`create_reminder_form.html` → `CreateReminderFormPage.robot`); when no evidence exists, from the screen name used in the flow steps.
- **Test case names**: follow `[profile: test_naming]` applied to the flow title; one test per logical flow unless the flow source splits it.
- **Preconditions**: a precondition shared by **all** tests in a suite goes in `Suite Setup` (chained with existing session setup via `Run Keywords … AND …`); a precondition specific to one test is its first step. A "data must exist" precondition is satisfied by creating that data via existing flow keywords, not assumed.
- **Parameterized locators** (one canonical pattern): declare the template with a `{placeholder}` token and resolve with `Format String`:

```robot
${ROW_BY_TITLE_TPL}    xpath=//ul[@id='items']//span[normalize-space()='{title}']

Get Row Locator
    [Documentation]    Resolve the row locator template for the given title.
    [Arguments]    ${title}
    ${locator}=    Format String    ${ROW_BY_TITLE_TPL}    title=${title}
    RETURN    ${locator}
```

